From 8c16766debc9809ecf2dcd251bc1609db5698ece Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 23:18:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/51] begonia-wifi (fwport): Stage-1 build wiring + BSP shim
 scaffold

Wire the vendor WMT/connsys (wmt_drv) + vendor BTIF forward-port into the
fork build under new configs:
  CONFIG_MTK_WMT_FWPORT (umbrella) / MTK_WMT_DRV / MTK_WMT_FWPORT_BTIF.

- drivers/misc/{Kconfig,Makefile}: source drivers/misc/mediatek/{Kconfig},
  descend into mediatek/ under CONFIG_MTK_WMT_FWPORT (alongside, not
  replacing, the reimpl CONFIG_MTK_BTIF mtk-btif.o).
- drivers/misc/mediatek/{Kconfig,Makefile}: umbrella config + descent.
- connectivity/{Kconfig,Makefile} + common/Makefile: wmt_drv object list
  (pruned Stage-1 set), all vendor BSP -I paths dropped, replaced with the
  fork-internal include dirs + the compat shim dir; force-include
  mtk-bsp-compat.h. -D macro set carried from the vendor Makefile.
- btif/{Kconfig,Makefile,common/Makefile}: vendor BTIF as mtk-vendor-btif.ko
  (disjoint module name + exported-symbol set from the reimpl mtk-btif.ko).
- compat/include: empty stub headers for the external MTK-BSP includes +
  initial mtk-bsp-compat.h (grown from build errors, not predicted).
- removed stale wmt_drv.mod.c build artifact.

No register address/value/bitfield touched (build-wiring + headers only).

Signed-off-by: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
